# === PRODUCTION auth (recommended): OAuth 2.0 client-credentials ===
# Works with a Connected App OR an External Client App (ECA) that has the
# client-credentials flow enabled and a least-privilege, read-only Run-As user.
# SF_LOGIN_URL MUST be the org's My Domain URL (NOT login.salesforce.com) for
# client-credentials, e.g. https://carhuborg.my.salesforce.com
SF_LOGIN_URL=https://YOUR-MYDOMAIN.my.salesforce.com
SF_CLIENT_ID=
SF_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# === DEV/TEST alternative: a pre-issued access token (e.g. from the sf CLI) ===
# If BOTH of these are set they take precedence over the client-credentials vars.
# Short-lived; never commit a real token.
SF_INSTANCE_URL=
SF_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#
SF_API_VERSION=v66.0
#
# Optional: protect the scanner's own API (X-API-Key). Unset = auth off (default for local dev).
# SCANNER_API_KEY=
